WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:08.939
"I don't understand why he's a tailor," Scrooge said, watching Dick Wilkins return to his stitching.

2
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:17.326
"Wilkins was no great business genius. But he worked hard and he had me as an example.

3
00:00:17.327 --> 00:00:22.471
He could have had a career in business and made a lot more money."

4
00:00:22.472 --> 00:00:28.518
"I suppose so," the Ghost of Christmas Present said

5
00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:35.115
"We must go. My time grows short, and we have more to see."

6
00:00:35.116 --> 00:00:41.372
Abruptly Scrooge found himself standing in front of an unfamiliar house.

7
00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:46.755
It was a humble place, smaller and shabbier even than Fred's.

8
00:00:46.756 --> 00:00:53.951
"Where are we?" Scrooge asked. "I don't recognize this place at all."

9
00:00:53.952 --> 00:01:01.151
"You will recognize the people who live here," the spirit replied.

10
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:05.079
They drifted in through the wall.

11
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.310
Inside was a woman wearing a dress that had been patched many times.

12
00:01:10.311 --> 00:01:15.467
She'd decorated it with new ribbons, probably to make it look more festive.

13
00:01:15.468 --> 00:01:21.881
Her daughter named Belinda was helping her mash potatoes in a rough wooden bowl.

14
00:01:21.882 --> 00:01:28.808
Nearby, a boy called Peter was laying out battered plates and forks on the table.

15
00:01:28.809 --> 00:01:35.749
"Who are these people?" Scrooge asked. "You said I would know them."

16
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:43.625
Suddenly the door flew open. A young boy and girl raced in with snow in their hair.

17
00:01:43.626 --> 00:01:47.355
"You're back, Sam and Sarah!" Peter said.

18
00:01:47.356 --> 00:01:50.589
"The church bells are ringing!" Sam cried.

19
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.505
"Yes, Father and Tiny Tim will be home soon," Sarah said.

20
00:01:55.506 --> 00:01:58.723
"Tiny Tim?" Scrooge said.

21
00:01:58.724 --> 00:02:03.392
"Oh! This must be Bob Cratchit's house."

22
00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:08.379
He looked at his companion for confirmation, but none was provided.

23
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.779
The spirit was watching a young woman hurry in after the children.

24
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.961
She was hardly out of her teens, with rosy cheeks.

25
00:02:16.962 --> 00:02:20.841
"Merry Christmas, Mother," she called happily.

26
00:02:20.842 --> 00:02:25.338
The woman dropped her fork and rushed to embrace her daughter.

27
00:02:25.339 --> 00:02:29.541
"Martha, my dear! I'm so happy you could come."

28
00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:32.667
"I wouldn't want to be anywhere else for Christmas."

29
00:02:32.668 --> 00:02:35.639
Martha hugged her tightly.

30
00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.276
Then she hugged Belinda and Peter.

31
00:02:38.277 --> 00:02:41.744
"You've both grown so tall!"

32
00:02:41.745 --> 00:02:46.074
Sam peeked out the front window.

33
00:02:46.075 --> 00:02:52.293
"Here come Father and Tiny Tim. Quick, Martha—hide! You can surprise them!"

34
00:02:52.294 --> 00:02:56.439
"Hide, Martha, hide!" Sarah said excitedly.

35
00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:03.455
The two younger children hurried Martha behind the coat rack while Peter and Belinda looked on with amusement.

36
00:03:03.456 --> 00:03:08.584
A moment later the door opened again to reveal Bob Cratchit.

37
00:03:08.585 --> 00:03:14.370
Tiny Tim was perched upon his shoulder, clutching his little wooden crutch as usual.

38
00:03:14.371 --> 00:03:21.706
"Merry Christmas, family!" Cratchit looked around.

39
00:03:21.707 --> 00:03:27.415
"Oh dear, where's our Martha? I thought she'd be here by now."

40
00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:30.801
Sam stifled a giggle.

41
00:03:30.802 --> 00:03:34.198
But then Martha stepped into view.

42
00:03:34.199 --> 00:03:38.341
"I can't stand to tease you, Father. Here I am!"

43
00:03:38.342 --> 00:03:44.639
Her father swung Tiny Tim to the ground, holding him steady while the boy got his crutch in place.

44
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.588
Then he hugged Martha tightly.

45
00:03:48.589 --> 00:03:53.036
"We're all here together," he said with a wide smile.

46
00:03:53.037 --> 00:03:56.776
"Now it feels like Christmas!"

47
00:03:56.777 --> 00:04:03.093
"The goose is almost ready, Tiny Tim," Belinda said. "Come and see!"

48
00:04:03.094 --> 00:04:08.926
Tim hobbled off after her, using his crutch to help himself along.

49
00:04:08.927 --> 00:04:12.913
Mrs. Cratchit watched him go.

50
00:04:12.914 --> 00:04:17.159
"And how was our little Tim?" she asked her husband quietly.

51
00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.278
"As good as gold," Cratchit said.

52
00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:26.933
"He never seems to mind that he can't do all of the things that other children do.

53
00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:33.155
He's happy watching the skaters, though he did ask about skating one day."

54
00:04:33.156 --> 00:04:36.076
Mrs. Cratchit took her husband's hand.

55
00:04:36.077 --> 00:04:42.159
"I'm happy just to have him still with us." Her voice was nearly a whisper.

56
00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:47.290
Then she cleared her throat and spoke loudly so that the children could hear her.

57
00:04:47.291 --> 00:04:54.061
"Now that your father's home, let's eat before the food gets cold!"

58
00:04:54.062 --> 00:04:57.978
The whole family sat down to enjoy the meal.

59
00:04:57.979 --> 00:05:04.105
Scrooge couldn't help observing that it was much more modest than the meals he'd seen elsewhere.

60
00:05:04.106 --> 00:05:07.770
The goose was so small, it looked more like a duck.

61
00:05:07.771 --> 00:05:12.739
There was hardly enough applesauce and mashed potatoes to go around.

62
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:17.645
But the family didn't seem to notice.

63
00:05:17.646 --> 00:05:22.638
"There was never a better goose than this one!" Bob said.

64
00:05:22.639 --> 00:05:26.776
"I've never tasted anything so flavorful."

65
00:05:26.777 --> 00:05:34.296
"Me neither," Peter said, helping himself to another piece.

66
00:05:34.297 --> 00:05:38.850
"And the potatoes are the best you've ever made, Mother!" Belinda said.

67
00:05:38.851 --> 00:05:44.256
Mrs. Cratchit beamed. "I was afraid I might have used too much salt."

68
00:05:44.257 --> 00:05:49.364
"Not at all," Martha said. "Everything is perfect."

69
00:05:49.365 --> 00:05:56.161
Bob smiled. "A Merry Christmas to us all, my dears."

70
00:05:56.162 --> 00:06:00.771
"Merry Christmas!" the family said together.

71
00:06:00.772 --> 00:06:12.906
Tiny Tim chimed in too. "God bless us, everyone."

